      "message": "I\u0027d change the arguments of from:\n\n`crec_flash_read_pstate_poweron_conf(uint8_t *buffer, int length)`\n\nTo `crec_flash_read_pstate_poweron_conf(struct persist_state* buf)`\n\nThen you can do a sizeof on the sizeof(struct persist_state) to extract the length. \n\nThis make it impossible to send the wrong size buffer back and forth, you could probably use it to replace the [CONFIG_POWERON_CONF_LEN] entry with just the struct.\n\nMagic number indexes are inevitably going to lead to problems over time and can be avoided in almost all cases.",
